      "message": "I\u0027m not sure I completely follow the flow here, so apologies if I\u0027m talking rubbish, but here goes:\n\n- If a device is using SWIOTLB, then the DMA transactions emitted by the device will target a SWIOTLB buffer\n\n- The DMA/SWIOTLB code then copies data to/from the SWIOTLB buffer into... where? The uncached heap, I presume?\n\nIn which case, using the uncached system heap is probably pointless and slow, as the CPU will bounce using a non-cacheable mapping. Furthermore, we still have `DMA_ATTR_SKIP_CPU_SYNC` set, so it\u0027s not clear to me that the SWIOTLB code will always do the right thing because (afaict), that will be cacheable and needs the cache maintenance (e.g. see `swiotlb_map()`).\n\nIs my understanding correct?",
